# Performance baseline (owner standard)

**Baseline date: 2026-08-04.** The live site’s current feel — smooth, responsive browse, snappy detail open, Team Builder that does not feel laggy — is the **minimum** bar. Every commit/update must **meet or beat** this standard. If a change makes anything feel worse, it is incomplete and needs more work (fix or revert) before shipping.

## What “good” means (must not regress)

1. **Cold / deploy** — Boot shell during DB load (`wsgi:application`). No long blank white page. After ready, browse lists paint without emptying out on `warming_up` (server may wait; client retries long enough).
2. **Browse first paint** — Characters/units lists feel immediate once warm. Eager-load only first-viewport thumbs (~16); keep frames/icons/below-fold lazy.
3. **Detail open** — Paint from API JSON quickly; do not await full portrait CDN warm. Warm ≤~12 images. No stuck/empty detail shells.
4. **Team Builder** — Stay in the main bundle unless the owner explicitly asks for a lazy split *and* UX stays as snappy as this baseline. Prior lazy-split was reverted for latency.
5. **Published/static data** — Lists + Top 10 BSP from precomputed caches. Never block user responses on live enrich/sim for board bumps.
6. **HTTP caching** — Stable JSON via `jsonify_cacheable` (ETag / 304). Prefer 304 over re-serializing.
7. **Images** — Game art via CDN + WebP (`IMAGE_CDN` / `imgUrl` / `convert_image_urls`). Do not pull portraits back onto Railway.
8. **Fonts** — Brand keeps FOTK. Locale-gate `@font-face`: EN cold load = Roboto + FOTK only; inject Noto/ShinGo/UDShinGo only for JA/TW/HK (`__GGEN_ENSURE_UI_FONTS__`). Keep `game_news.html` in sync. Never demote brand title to system-first.

## Change discipline

- Prefer **one measured lever at a time**; smoke before ship.
- After any server/UI change: spot-check `/`, `/health`, `/api/characters`, detail open, and (if touched) Team Builder.
- **Do not** re-land optimistic detail / View Transitions / service worker / Calculator·DC or Ranking lazy splits without an explicit owner ask + verification.
- `node --check static/js/app.js` before shipping large JS edits; rebuild `app.min.js` when `app.js` changes.

## Anti-patterns (regressions)

- Exhausting short warmup retries so browse stays empty after deploy
- Flooding CDN with eager thumbs for every list row
- Blocking gunicorn bind / `/health` on stage prewarm or heavy sync work
- Lazy-loading Team Builder (or other hot tools) in a way that adds open lag
- Nested-quote `outerHTML` inside template-literal `onerror` on huge `app.js` lines
- Demoting brand fonts to system-first “for performance”
- Registering all CJK `@font-face` on every cold EN load (~19MB)
